================================================================================
MIGRATION SUMMARY LOG
SQL Server to PostgreSQL Migration for ADO.NET Core Application
Date: 2026-04-11
================================================================================

1. MIGRATION OVERVIEW
---------------------
Source Database: Microsoft SQL Server 2019
Target Database: PostgreSQL 13
Application Framework: .NET 9.0 with ADO.NET
Migration Tool: AWS DMS MCP (attempted), Manual conversion (applied)

2. SQL STATEMENTS PROCESSED
----------------------------
Total statements: 7
Successfully converted by DMS: 0 (DMS returned errors for all statements)
Manually converted: 7 (with lowercase schema object naming)
DMS Error: "Metadata model creation failed: {'error': 'Unknown metadata model creation status: RECEIVED'}"

Statement 1 - GetAllProductsAsync:
  Type: SELECT with CTE, Window Functions (AVG OVER, COUNT OVER), CASE, ROUND, INNER JOIN
  Conversion: Lowercase schema objects only (SQL syntax already PostgreSQL-compatible)

Statement 2 - GetProductByIdAsync:
  Type: SELECT with CTE, LAG Window Function, CASE, ROUND, LEFT JOIN
  Conversion: Lowercase schema objects only
  Parameters: @ProductId

Statement 3 - InsertProductAsync:
  Type: Transaction block with INSERT, SCOPE_IDENTITY(), GETDATE(), UPDATE
  Conversion: SCOPE_IDENTITY() -> RETURNING; GETDATE() -> NOW(); 
  Restructured from single SQL batch to multiple C# NpgsqlCommand calls within transaction
  Parameters: @Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity

Statement 4 - UpdateProductAsync:
  Type: Transaction block with DECLARE, SELECT INTO variables, UPDATE, INSERT, UPDATE
  Conversion: GETDATE() -> NOW(); DECLARE variables -> C# variables
  Restructured from single SQL batch to multiple C# NpgsqlCommand calls within transaction
  Parameters: @ProductId, @Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity

Statement 5 - DeleteProductAsync:
  Type: Transaction block with DECLARE, SELECT INTO variables, INSERT, DELETE, UPDATE with CASE
  Conversion: GETDATE() -> NOW(); DECLARE variables -> C# variables
  Restructured from single SQL batch to multiple C# NpgsqlCommand calls within transaction
  Parameters: @ProductId

Statement 6 - GetProductsByPriceRangeAsync:
  Type: SELECT with CTE, RANK() OVER, PERCENT_RANK() OVER, BETWEEN, CASE
  Conversion: Lowercase schema objects only
  Parameters: @MinPrice, @MaxPrice

Statement 7 - GetLowStockProductsAsync:
  Type: SELECT with CTE, AVG/MIN/MAX OVER(), CASE, ROUND
  Conversion: Lowercase schema objects; added ::numeric cast for integer division
  Parameters: @Threshold

3. SQL EQUIVALENCY VALIDATION
-------------------------------
Tool Used: sql-equivalency___validate_sql_equivalence
Results: All 7 statement pairs returned ERROR (tool internal error: "'uniqueID'")
Report: sql_equivalency_validation_report.json

4. CODE CHANGES
---------------

4.1 ProductRepository.cs (sourceCode/DataAccess/ProductRepository.cs):
  - using Microsoft.Data.SqlClient -> using Npgsql
  - SqlConnection -> NpgsqlConnection (3 occurrences)
  - SqlCommand -> NpgsqlCommand (15 occurrences)
  - SqlDataReader -> NpgsqlDataReader (1 occurrence)
  - 7 SQL Server SQL statements replaced with PostgreSQL equivalents
  - Transaction methods restructured for PostgreSQL compatibility

4.2 AdoCore.csproj (sourceCode/AdoCore.csproj):
  - Removed: <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Data.SqlClient" Version="5.1.4" />
  - Added: <PackageReference Include="Npgsql" Version="8.0.1" />

4.3 appsettings.json (sourceCode/appsettings.json):
  - DevConnection: Server=localhost;Database=ProductManagement;Trusted_Connection=True;MultipleActiveResultSets=true;TrustServerCertificate=True
    -> Host=localhost;Database=ProductManagement;Username=postgres;Password=postgres
  - ProdConnection: Same transformation applied

4.4 README.md (sourceCode/README.md):
  - Updated all SQL Server references to PostgreSQL
  - Updated prerequisites (PostgreSQL 13+, pgAdmin)
  - Updated connection string examples
  - Updated NuGet package list (Microsoft.Data.SqlClient -> Npgsql)
  - Updated troubleshooting section

